  <h2><a href="/web/20110102191514/http://roblox.zendesk.com/forums">Answers</a><span class="delim">/</span><a href="/web/20110102191514/http://roblox.zendesk.com/forums/202642-technical-issues">Technical Issues</a></h2>

  <div class="frame">
    <div class="entry nobottom" style="padding-bottom:0;">
      <h3 class="entry-title">New GUI Problems</h3>
      <p class="sub">Reese Dec-02 2010</p>
      <div class="user_formatted" style="margin-top:35px;">
        <p>Problem: The new GUI is preventing play in your place.&nbsp; (December 2, 2010)</p>
<p>Answer: We have tracked down the source of the user GUI bug that slipped our  unintentionally in this morning's release. We are working on a fix, which will  be up on gametest.roblox.com in a couple of hours (you can help us test if if  you want) and probably released by tomorrow morning. <br/><br/>SCRIPTERS:  <br/><br/>Don't change your places. They will work after we push the fix.  <br/><br/>For those who really want to know, this is what happened. Previously  when you put ScreenGui elements in the Workspace, they would NOT render. The  client team did some code consolidation and refactoring, and as a side effect,  they accidentally made ScreenGui elements in the Workspace render. Whoops!</p>
<p>-Telamon</p>
      </div>
      
    </div>
  </div>
